{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is an equilateral triangle. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d383bb3a27b6ea0b2b4bb30d5478e50fed47f4ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(175); usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;); defaultpen(TimesRoman());  defaultpen(linewidth(1.1bp)); defaultpen(fontsize(12pt));  draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(1,sqrt(3))--(0,0));  label(&quot;$P$&quot;, (1+0.04,sqrt(3)+0.1)); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, (0-0.08,0-0.07)); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, (2+0.07,0-0.06)); label(&quot;$4x$&quot;, (0.5-0.1,sqrt(3)/2+0.15)); label(&quot;$x+12$&quot;, (1.5+0.21,sqrt(3)/2+0.15)); [/asy]\" width=\"295\" height=\"265\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6571d68cca8decb312cecd20d36a6f5c3347eefb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c3b4b8a548881e5211fe9327c861090c4ebe42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef4be1f65eee4365b01cbdcc25bd8827b3987f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 48 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 32 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because all of the side lengths of an equilateral triangle are equal, we can equate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6571d68cca8decb312cecd20d36a6f5c3347eefb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c3b4b8a548881e5211fe9327c861090c4ebe42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = x + 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\t4x &amp;= x+12\\\\\n\t3x &amp;= 12\\\\\n\tx &amp;= \\dfrac{12}{3} = \\boxed{{\\textbf {(C)}\\ 4}}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" ro